## Change Summary

| Area | Change |
|---|---|
| **Data** | Added `showImageOptimizationModal`, `pendingPasteImage`, `imageOptimizationPreviewUrl`, `imageOptimizationProcessing`, `imageOptimizationSettings` (max dimension 1536, quality 0.85) |
| **Template** | Added DaisyUI modal for pasted image with sliders for max dimension/quality, live preview, original size, and **Attach Optimized** button |
| **`prepareAttachmentFromFile`** | Now calls `resizeImageIfNeeded` before `ChatAttachment.fromFile` (applies to uploads/drops) |
| **`prepareAttachmentFromUrl`** | Now also resizes URL-based images automatically |
| **`onContentPaste`** | Instead of immediately attaching clipboard image, opens the optimization modal |
| **New methods** | `resizeImageIfNeeded`, `formatFileSize`, `openImageOptimizationModal`, `closeImageOptimizationModal`, `confirmImageOptimization` |

**Key behavior:**  
- Pasting an image opens a modal where the user can adjust max dimension (512–4096px) and JPEG quality (50–100%).  
- Confirming runs a canvas-based resize/re-encode and attaches the optimized image.  
- Other image paths (drag-drop, file picker, URL paste) silently auto-optimize with the same default settings.

## Direct Recommendation

Add a dedicated **Image Editor Modal** that opens both for newly pasted images and for any existing image attachment. The editor provides:

- **Quality slider** (50–100%) for JPEG re-encoding
- **Max dimension slider** (512–4096px) for downscaling
- **Rotation** (90° left/right)
- **Flip** (horizontal/vertical)
- **Crop** via a draggable rectangular selection

When the user confirms, the edited image replaces the original attachment (or adds a new one) and the updated attachment is saved with the message once sent. The editor integrates with the existing paste flow and adds an `@edit-attachment` event to `ChatAttachmentPreview` so users can edit already attached images.

