### 5. Add edit event listener on attachment preview

Update the `ChatAttachmentPreview` usage in the template to listen for an `edit-attachment` event (assumed to be emitted by the child component).

```vue src/components/chat/Chat.vue
<ChatAttachmentPreview
  :attachments="attachments"
  @remove-attachment="removeAttachment"
  @edit-attachment="editAttachment"
  v-if="attachments?.length && !composerCollapsed"
/>
```

### 6. Modify `resizeImageIfNeeded` (optional but recommended)

If you still want automatic resizing for other image paths (drag-drop, URL), keep the existing `resizeImageIfNeeded` or use the new `processEditedImage` with default transformations. For simplicity, keep `resizeImageIfNeeded` and use it in `prepareAttachmentFromFile` and `prepareAttachmentFromUrl`.

---

## Change Summary

| Area | Change |
|---|---|
| **Template** | Replaced optimization modal with full image editor (crop, rotate, flip, sliders). Added `@edit-attachment` event binding. |
| **Data** | Added `editingAttachmentIndex`, `imageEditorRotation`, `imageEditorFlipH/V`, `showCropOverlay`, `cropRect` and related drag state. |
| **Methods** | Added `openImageEditor`, `closeImageOptimizationModal`, `imagePreviewStyle`, `rotateImage`, `flipImage`, `resetImageTransformations`, `toggleCropMode`, `startCrop`, `updateCrop`, `endCrop`, `cropOverlayStyle`, `processEditedImage`, `confirmImageOptimization`, `editAttachment`. |
| **Paste flow** | `onContentPaste` now calls `openImageEditor` instead of directly attaching. |
| **`prepareAttachmentFromFile` / `prepareAttachmentFromUrl`** | Still use `resizeImageIfNeeded` for automatic optimization (unchanged). |

---

## Required Change in `ChatAttachmentPreview.vue`

To enable editing existing attachments, the `ChatAttachmentPreview` component **must emit an `edit-attachment` event** with the index of the clicked attachment. Example:

```vue
<!-- Inside ChatAttachmentPreview.vue, for each image attachment -->
<button
  class="absolute top-1 right-1 btn btn-xs btn-circle btn-ghost"
  @click.stop="$emit('edit-attachment', index)"
>
  <i class="fa-solid fa-pen"></i>
</button>
```

Place this button inside each attachment’s preview container and ensure the parent `<Chat.vue>` listens as shown above.

---

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- ❌ **Not revoking object URLs** – Always call `URL.revokeObjectURL` in `closeImageOptimizationModal` to prevent memory leaks.
- ❌ **Forgetting to reset editor state** – Reset rotation/flip/crop after each use so a new edit starts fresh.
- ❌ **Blocking the UI during canvas processing** – The processing is async and uses `createImageBitmap`, but for very large images it may still cause jank; consider adding a loading indicator.
- ❌ **Ignoring the `editingAttachmentIndex`** – Ensure you distinguish between adding a new paste vs. replacing an existing index.

---

## Accessibility Checklist

- [ ] Modal is keyboard navigable (focus trap, Escape to close).
- [ ] All icon buttons have `aria-label` (the code above uses icons; add appropriate labels if needed).
- [ ] Crop overlay does not break keyboard users (provide alternative numeric inputs if needed).
- [ ] Color contrast for sliders and buttons meets WCAG AA.
- [ ] Loading state (`imageOptimizationProcessing`) disables the confirm button and shows progress.

---

## Implementation Steps

1. Apply the above changes to `src/components/chat/Chat.vue`.
2. Modify `ChatAttachmentPreview.vue` to emit `edit-attachment` when an edit icon is clicked.
3. Test the paste flow: paste an image → editor opens → adjust quality/dimension/crop/rotation → confirm → attachment appears with edited image.
4. Test editing an existing attachment: click the edit icon on a thumbnail → editor opens with the image → make changes → confirm → thumbnail updates.
5. Send a message containing an edited image to verify the attachment is saved and sent correctly.

